The provided code is a part of the `UnitOfWorkDbContextProvider` class in the `Volo.Abp.EntityFrameworkCore` namespace. The `CreateDbContextWithTransaction` method is used to create a database context with a transaction. If the transaction is not supported by the database, it logs a warning message using the `Logger` property.

To write unit tests for this method, you can use the `xunit` framework and `Moq` library to mock the dependencies. Here's an example test class:

```csharp
using Xunit;
using Moq;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using Volo.Abp.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Volo.Abp.Uow.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace Volo.Abp.Uow.EntityFrameworkCore.Tests
{
    public class UnitOfWorkDbContextProviderTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void CreateDbContextWithTransaction_LogsWarning_WhenTransactionsAreNotSupported()
        {
            // Arrange
            var unitOfWorkMock = new Mock<IUnitOfWork>();
            var loggerMock = new Mock<ILogger<UnitOfWorkDbContextProvider<MyDbContext>>>();
            var provider = new UnitOfWorkDbContextProvider<MyDbContext>(unitOfWorkMock.Object, loggerMock.Object);

            // Act
            provider.CreateDbContextWithTransaction(unitOfWorkMock.Object);

            // Assert
            loggerMock.Verify(logger => logger.LogWarning(It.IsAny<string>()), Times.Once);
        }

        private class MyDbContext : IEfCoreDbContext
        {
            public DbSet<MyEntity> MyEntities { get; set; }

            public Task<int> SaveChangesAsync(CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
            {
                throw new NotImplementedException();
            }
        }

        private class MyEntity
        {
        }
    }
}
```

This test class has a single test method `CreateDbContextWithTransaction_LogsWarning_WhenTransactionsAreNotSupported` that tests the `CreateDbContextWithTransaction` method. It creates a mock `IUnitOfWork` object and a mock `ILogger` object, and then creates an instance of the `UnitOfWorkDbContextProvider` class with these mocks. The test method then calls the `CreateDbContextWithTransaction` method and verifies that the `Logger` logs a warning message using the `Verify` method.

Note that this test class uses a custom `MyDbContext` class that implements the `IEfCoreDbContext` interface, and a custom `MyEntity` class that is used as the entity type in the `MyDbContext` class. You can replace these with your own custom classes or use existing classes in your project.

Also, make sure to install the required NuGet packages, including `xunit`, `xunit.runner.visualstudio`, `Moq`, and `Microsoft.Extensions.Logging`, and configure the test project to use the `xunit` test framework.
